# Business Rules (Invariants) — TokenRealty

**Full spec:** [docs/BUSINESS_RULES.md](../../docs/BUSINESS_RULES.md) — read before money, marketplace, payment, or Kafka work.

Detail by area: [payment-ledger.mdc](payment-ledger.mdc), [investment-limits.mdc](investment-limits.mdc), [kafka-messaging.mdc](kafka-messaging.mdc), [business-exception.mdc](business-exception.mdc).

## Never violate

- **Ledger:** immutable `LedgerEntry` rows; corrections = reversal/compensating entries — [payment-ledger.mdc](payment-ledger.mdc)
- **Idempotency:** same `Idempotency-Key` → same payment result; different payload → 409
- **Kafka consumers:** dedupe by `eventId` (`KafkaEventConsumer` + `processed_events`)
- **Outbox:** enqueue in same TX as domain write; never `KafkaTemplate.send` inside open business TX — [kafka-messaging.mdc](kafka-messaging.mdc)
- **KYC before match:** Compliance check before matched order / escrow — [investment-limits.mdc](investment-limits.mdc)
- **Escrow before transfer release:** release only after `transfer.completed`
- **Token stock:** never exceed `tokensAvailable`; PRIMARY sell-out → Registry `FULLY_SOLD`
- **Registry authority:** flat/building/SPV/document metadata lives in Property Registry; Document Service pins IPFS then registers CID
- **Secrets:** no private keys, seeds, or KYC doc bodies in logs or Kafka payloads
- **Errors:** typed exceptions → ProblemDetail; not generic 500 for business rejections — [business-exception.mdc](business-exception.mdc)
- **Status transitions:** via domain services (`updateStatus`, entity methods) — not raw enum assignment from controllers

## Buy flow order (do not reorder)

```text
KYC → reserve tokens + match → escrow → payment.confirmed → transfer → transfer.completed → release escrow → trade.settled
```

## Trust nothing external

Idempotent · auditable · reversible (where possible) · reconcilable
